<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bonos were lower in late trade on Wednesday, tracking other European bonds and weaker Treasuries amid worries of a sell-off in U.S. assets.</p>
<p>At home, dealers were eyeing October PPI data tomorrow. &quot;It'll give a good idea on whether we can reasonably expect an improvement in the CPI in the coming months,&quot; said one.</p>
<p>Interest in the market continues weighted in the middle part of the yield curve, he added. But the short end of the curve is discounting &quot;very agressive rate cuts,&quot; ahead of the Bank of Spain repo auction on Friday, he said.</p>
</text>
